From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] includes: guard unused x86 intrinsic headers

system_includes.h unconditionally includes the SSE and SSE2 headers even
though the Milton 1.9.1 source does not use their types or intrinsics. Those
headers exist only on x86 targets. Keep them available for x86 builds and do
not include them on RISC-V or other architectures.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of Milton 1.9.1 src/system_includes.h
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
---
 src/system_includes.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/system_includes.h b/src/system_includes.h
--- a/src/system_includes.h
+++ b/src/system_includes.h
@@ -43,0 +44 @@
+#if defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__) || defined(_M_IX86) || defined(_M_X64)
@@ -45,0 +47 @@
+#endif
